0,Ahamb language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ahamb_language,"Ahamb’s phonology is characterised by distinctive prenasalisation in its plosives and trills. There are three contrastive trills, including the typologically rare plain bilabial trill. [7] The vowel inventory is also relatively large compared to other related languages, with eight contrastive vowels.",Axamb,Austronesian
